Fundamentals of Vacuum Physics and Technology — Eshraq Al-Dmour (@gas-cas-fundamentals: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gas-sources) { r_175RE9FCKASP84H5VPDDPDX0C9
Eshraq Al-Dmour. *Fundamentals of Vacuum Physics and Technology*, contribution to the 2017 CERN Accelerator School, author manuscript published in 2020, 21 pages. [Versioned record](https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.01464v1), [complete paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.01464).

Read the full paper, deriving the kinetic, conductance and pumping relations. Use it to move from handbook calculations to vacuum research. For every formula, identify geometry, gas state, reflection assumptions and units. The transparent thin-aperture conductance needs a transmission correction for finite thickness; a long-tube approximation has its own geometric limit.

Metadata and selected conductance, effective pumping and gas-source passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. The full manuscript was downloaded outside the repository. The arXiv licence grants distribution by arXiv, not unrestricted adaptation. The entire 374-page CERN school proceedings was identified, but its direct download returned an access challenge; these individually available author manuscripts provide usable readings without claiming that the whole proceedings was inspected.

